(   - N2 transfers two electrons to bound Ubiquinone \(Q\) in the catalytic pocket at the arm) Tj
T*
(   interface, reducing it to ubiquinol \(QH2\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Long-Range Conformational Proton Pumping:) Tj
T*
(   - Complex I pumps 4 H+ across the membrane for every 2 electrons transferred.) Tj
T*
(   - Reduction of Q induces negative charge accumulation, triggering electrostatic rearrangements) Tj
T*
(   that drive a piston-like horizontal alpha-helix \(HL helix\) spanning the entire length of the) Tj
T*
(   membrane arm.) Tj
T*
(   - Movement of this central coupling rod coordinates the simultaneous tilting of discontinuous) Tj
T*
(   transmembrane helices in ND1, ND2, ND4, and ND5, opening four proton-translocating channels and) Tj
T*
(   pumping 4 H+ from matrix to IMS.) Tj
