(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Q-Cycle mechanism of Complex III \(Cytochrome bc1 Complex\) and its role in bifurcated electron transfer.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Q-Cycle Mechanism in Complex III:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Biochemical Conundrum:) Tj
T*
(   Ubiquinol \(QH2\) is an obligatory two-electron carrier, whereas the downstream electron) Tj
T*
(   acceptor, Cytochrome c, is a strictly one-electron carrier. Complex III resolves this via Peter) Tj
T*
(   Mitchell's Q-cycle using two distinct ubiquinone binding sites:) Tj
T*
(   - Qo Site: Located near the outer \(IMS\) face of the inner membrane.) Tj
T*
(   - Qi Site: Located near the inner \(matrix\) face.) Tj
T*
(   2. Step 1 \(First Oxidation Cycle at Qo\):) Tj
T*
(   - A QH2 molecule binds to the Qo site and transfers its first electron to the high-potential) Tj
T*
(   chain: Rieske [2Fe-2S] cluster -> Cytochrome c1 -> Cytochrome c \(which dissociates to deliver) Tj
T*
(   its electron to Complex IV\).) Tj
T*
(   - This leaves an unstable, highly reactive ubisemiquinone radical \(Q.-\) at the Qo site.) Tj
T*
(   - The semiquinone immediately dumps its second electron into the low-potential chain:) Tj
T*
(   Cytochrome b_L \(low potential\) -> Cytochrome b_H \(high potential\) -> bound oxidized Q at the Qi) Tj
T*
(   site, reducing it to a stable semiquinone radical \(Q.-_i\).) Tj
T*
(   - Simultaneously, two protons \(2 H+\) are released into the intermembrane space.) Tj
T*
(   3. Step 2 \(Second Oxidation Cycle at Qo\):) Tj
T*
(   - A second QH2 binds the Qo site and undergoes identical bifurcated oxidation.) Tj
T*
(   - The first electron reduces a second Cytochrome c.) Tj
T*
(   - The second electron travels down b_L -> b_H to the semiquinone \(Q.-_i\) at the Qi site.) Tj
T*
(   - The Qi site takes up two protons \(2 H+\) from the mitochondrial matrix, fully reducing it to) Tj
T*
(   regenerate one molecule of QH2.) Tj
T*
(   4. Net Stoichiometry of the Q-Cycle:) Tj
T*
(   - Two QH2 oxidized at Qo - One QH2 regenerated at Qi = Net 1 QH2 oxidized.) Tj
T*
(   - Two Cytochrome c molecules reduced.) Tj
T*
(   - Four protons \(4 H+\) extruded into the intermembrane space.) Tj
T*
(   - Two protons \(2 H+\) consumed from the mitochondrial matrix.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
