/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the molecular architecture, catalytic centers, and proton translocation mechanism of Complex IV \(Cytochrome c Oxidase\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Structure and Catalysis of Complex IV \(Cytochrome c Oxidase\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Subunit and Cofactor Organization:) Tj
T*
(   Complex IV is a homodimeric multi-subunit terminal oxidase embedded in the inner membrane. In) Tj
T*
(   mammals, each monomer consists of 13 subunits and four redox metal centers:) Tj
T*
(   - Cu_A Center: A binuclear mixed-valence copper center [Cu\(1.5+\)...Cu\(1.5+\)] located in the) Tj
T*
