(   periplasmic domain of Subunit II.) Tj
T*
(   - Heme a: A low-spin six-coordinate heme located in Subunit I.) Tj
T*
(   - Binuclear Catalytic Center \(Heme a3 - Cu_B\): Located in Subunit I, forming the active) Tj
T*
(   oxygen-binding pocket.) Tj
T*
(   2. Sequential Four-Electron Transfer Pathway:) Tj
T*
(   - Four consecutive molecules of reduced Cytochrome c bind to the IMS face of Subunit II,) Tj
T*
(   delivering one electron at a time:) Tj
T*
(   Cytochrome c -> Cu_A -> Heme a -> Heme a3 - Cu_B center.) Tj
T*
(   - In the fully reduced state [Fe\(II\) - Cu\(I\)], molecular oxygen \(O2\) binds between Heme a3 and) Tj
T*
(   Cu_B.) Tj
T*
(   - Rapid electron transfer forms a peroxy bridge [Fe\(III\)-O-O-Cu\(II\)], which is homolytically) Tj
T*
(   cleaved without releasing toxic reactive oxygen intermediates.) Tj
T*
(   - Addition of four chemical protons \(4 H+_matrix\) reduces the two bound oxygen atoms completely) Tj
T*
(   to two molecules of water \(2 H2O\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Vectorial Proton Pumping:) Tj
T*
(   - In addition to consuming 4 chemical protons from the matrix to make 2 H2O, Complex IV pumps) Tj
T*
(   four additional protons \(4 H+_pumped\) across the membrane through two proton channels \(the) Tj
T*
(   D-channel and K-channel\):) Tj
T*
(   4 Cyt c\(red\) + 8 H+_matrix + O2 -> 4 Cyt c\(ox\) + 2 H2O + 4 H+_IMS.) Tj
T*
(   - Yields a net translocation of 2 pumped protons per pair of electrons.) Tj
