(   2. ATP Synthase Inhibitors \(e.g., Oligomycin\):) Tj
T*
(   - Mechanism: A macrolide antibiotic that binds specifically to the contact interface between) Tj
T*
(   subunit a and the c-ring of the F0 sector.) Tj
T*
(   - Action: Physically plugs the proton translocation channel, mechanically preventing c-ring) Tj
T*
(   rotation and proton re-entry into the matrix.) Tj
T*
(   - Effects on Bioenergetics:) Tj
T*
(   - ATP synthesis is directly and completely blocked.) Tj
T*
(   - Protons pumped by ETC accumulate in the IMS without release; the proton motive force rises to) Tj
T*
(   a high thermodynamic equilibrium ceiling \(~ -220 mV\).) Tj
T*
(   - This massive proton back-pressure halts further proton pumping by Complexes I, III, and IV,) Tj
T*
(   causing respiration \(O2 consumption\) to drop to near zero.) Tj
T*
(   - Diagnostic Test: Adding an uncoupler \(2,4-DNP\) to oligomycin-inhibited mitochondria) Tj
T*
