(   = -0.32 V\) against a thermodynamic gradient of 1.14 V, driven by the sequential absorption of) Tj
T*
(   two photons at two distinct photosystems \(PSII and PSI\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Step 1 \(Photosystem II & Water Splitting\):) Tj
T*
(   - A photon \(680 nm\) excites the reaction center chlorophyll P680 to P680* \(E0' = -0.80 V\).) Tj
T*
(   - Excited P680* rapidly ejects an electron to Pheophytin \(Pheo\), becoming the extraordinarily) Tj
T*
(   strong oxidant P680+ \(E0' = +1.25 V\).) Tj
T*
(   - P680+ extracts an electron from a redox-active tyrosine residue \(Tyr_Z\), which in turn) Tj
T*
(   extracts electrons from the Mn4CaO5 Oxygen-Evolving Complex \(OEC\).) Tj
T*
(   - Four successive oxidation steps \(Kok's S-state cycle\) split 2 H2O molecules into 4 H+, 4) Tj
T*
(   electrons, and 1 molecule of O2 in the thylakoid lumen.) Tj
T*
(   3. Step 2 \(Plastoquinone Pool & Cytochrome b6f\):) Tj
T*
(   - From Pheophytin, electrons transfer to tightly bound Plastoquinone A \(QA\), then to mobile) Tj
T*
(   Plastoquinone B \(QB\).) Tj
T*
(   - Upon receiving 2 electrons and 2 protons from the stroma, QB is reduced to Plastoquinol) Tj
T*
(   \(PQH2\), which enters the thylakoid lipid bilayer.) Tj
T*
(   - PQH2 transfers electrons through the Cytochrome b6f complex via a Q-cycle analogous to) Tj
T*
(   mitochondrial Complex III, pumping 4 H+ per 2 electrons into the thylakoid lumen.) Tj
T*
(   4. Step 3 \(Plastocyanin to Photosystem I\):) Tj
T*
(   - Cytochrome b6f passes electrons to Plastocyanin \(PC\), a water-soluble copper protein) Tj
T*
(   diffusing in the thylakoid lumen.) Tj
T*
(   - PC donates its electron to oxidized P700+ in Photosystem I.) Tj
T*
(   5. Step 4 \(Photosystem I to NADP+\):) Tj
T*
(   - Absorption of a second photon \(700 nm\) excites P700 to P700*, ejecting an electron through a) Tj
T*
(   chain: A0 \(chlorophyll a\) -> A1 \(phylloquinone / vitamin K1\) -> FeS clusters \(FX, FA, FB\).) Tj
T*
(   - From FB, electrons reduce Ferredoxin \(Fd\), a soluble stromal [2Fe-2S] protein.) Tj
T*
(   - Ferredoxin-NADP+ Reductase \(FNR\) catalyzes the transfer of two electrons from two reduced) Tj
T*
(   ferredoxin molecules plus a stromal proton to NADP+, yielding NADPH.) Tj
