(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the catalytic mechanism and Oxygenase-Carboxylase duality of Rubisco, detailing the metabolic pathway of Photorespiration \(C2 Cycle\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Rubisco Catalysis and the Photorespiratory C2 Cycle:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Dual Carboxylase-Oxygenase Activity:) Tj
T*
(   Ribulose-1,5-bisphosphate carboxylase/oxygenase \(Rubisco\) is a hexadecameric enzyme \(L8S8, 550) Tj
T*
(   kDa\). Its catalytic active site cannot completely discriminate between CO2 and O2 because both) Tj
T*
(   are linear, non-polar gases:) Tj
T*
(   - Carboxylase Reaction \(Calvin Cycle\): RuBP \(5C\) enolizes into an enediolate intermediate that) Tj
T*
(   attacks CO2, forming an unstable 6C intermediate cleaved into two molecules of) Tj
T*
(   3-Phosphoglycerate \(3-PGA\).) Tj
T*
(   - Oxygenase Reaction \(Photorespiration\): The enediolate intermediate attacks O2 instead,) Tj
T*
(   forming a hydroperoxide intermediate cleaved into one molecule of 3-PGA \(3C\) and one molecule) Tj
T*
(   of 2-Phosphoglycolate \(2C\).) Tj
T*
(   2. The Photorespiratory Salvage Pathway \(C2 Cycle across 3 Organelles\):) Tj
T*
(   - Chloroplast: Phosphoglycolate phosphatase cleaves 2-phosphoglycolate to Glycolate, which is) Tj
T*
(   transported out.) Tj
T*
(   - Peroxisome: Glycolate oxidase oxidizes glycolate to Glyoxylate, generating toxic H2O2) Tj
T*
(   \(destroyed by catalase\). Glutamate:glyoxylate aminotransferase converts glyoxylate into the) Tj
T*
(   amino acid Glycine.) Tj
T*
(   - Mitochondria: Two molecules of glycine enter the matrix. The Glycine Decarboxylase Complex) Tj
T*
(   \(GDC\) and Serine Hydroxymethyltransferase \(SHMT\) convert 2 Glycine -> 1 Serine + CO2 + NH3 +) Tj
T*
(   NADH. This step loses 25% of the fixed carbon as CO2!) Tj
T*
(   - Peroxisome & Chloroplast: Serine returns to the peroxisome, transaminating to) Tj
T*
