T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Glyoxylate Cycle and Lipid-to-Carbohydrate Conversion:) Tj
T*
(   1. Biological Significance:) Tj
T*
(   Animals cannot achieve net synthesis of glucose from fatty acids because the two carbons) Tj
T*
(   entering the TCA cycle as Acetyl-CoA are completely lost as two molecules of CO2 in the) Tj
T*
(   isocitrate dehydrogenase and alpha-ketoglutarate dehydrogenase reactions.) Tj
T*
(   Germinating oilseeds \(e.g., castor bean, sunflower\) bypass these decarboxylation steps via the) Tj
T*
(   Glyoxylate Cycle, converting stored seed oil \(triacylglycerols\) into sucrose to fuel seedling) Tj
T*
