(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the biophysical and chemical mechanisms of Reactive Oxygen Species \(ROS\) generation by the respiratory chain and their enzymatic detoxification.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Mitochondrial Reactive Oxygen Species \(ROS\) Generation and Antioxidant Defenses:) Tj
T*
(   1. Chemical Mechanisms of ROS Generation:) Tj
T*
(   Under normal aerobic conditions, approximately 0.2% to 2.0% of total oxygen consumed by) Tj
T*
(   mitochondria undergoes incomplete one-electron reduction to generate the Superoxide anion) Tj
T*
(   radical \(O2.-\):) Tj
T*
(   - Complex I \(NADH site & flavin\): Low forward electron transfer or reverse electron transport) Tj
T*
(   \(RET\) driven by a high proton motive force reduces FMN, leaking electrons directly to dissolved) Tj
T*
(   O2.) Tj
T*
(   - Complex III \(Qo site\): The unstable semiquinone radical \(Q.-\) intermediate formed during the) Tj
T*
(   Q-cycle can accidentally donate its unpaired electron to O2 in the outer leaflet/IMS.) Tj
T*
(   2. Secondary ROS Formation:) Tj
T*
(   - Superoxide itself has limited reactivity but dismutates into Hydrogen Peroxide \(H2O2\).) Tj
T*
(   - In the presence of trace transition metals \(Fe2+ or Cu+\), H2O2 undergoes the non-enzymatic) Tj
T*
(   Fenton Reaction:) Tj
T*
(   Fe2+ + H2O2 -> Fe3+ + OH. \(Hydroxyl radical\) + OH-.) Tj
T*
(   - The hydroxyl radical \(OH.\) is the most reactive macromolecular oxidant known, causing) Tj
T*
(   catastrophic lipid peroxidation, DNA double-strand breaks, and protein carbonylation.) Tj
T*
(   3. Enzymatic Antioxidant Defense Hierarchy:) Tj
T*
(   - Superoxide Dismutase \(SOD\): Catalyzes the conversion of superoxide to hydrogen peroxide:) Tj
T*
(   2 O2.- + 2 H+ -> H2O2 + O2.) Tj
T*
(   Isoforms: Manganese-SOD \(Mn-SOD / SOD2\) in mitochondrial matrix; Copper-Zinc SOD \(Cu/Zn-SOD /) Tj
T*
(   SOD1\) in cytoplasm and IMS.) Tj
T*
(   - Catalase: Heme-containing enzyme localized in peroxisomes that decomposes H2O2:) Tj
T*
(   2 H2O2 -> 2 H2O + O2.) Tj
T*
(   - Glutathione Peroxidase \(GPx\): Selenocysteine-containing enzyme in matrix and cytosol that) Tj
T*
(   reduces H2O2 to water using reduced glutathione \(GSH\):) Tj
T*
(   H2O2 + 2 GSH -> GSSG + 2 H2O.) Tj
T*
(   Glutathione Reductase \(GR\) regenerates GSH from GSSG using NADPH produced by the pentose) Tj
T*
(   phosphate pathway or nicotinamide nucleotide transhydrogenase.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
