(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the structural organization and endosymbiotic origins of Mitochondria and Chloroplasts, presenting modern phylogenetic evidence.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Endosymbiotic Origins and Organellar Ultrastructure:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Endosymbiotic Theory \(Lynn Margulis, 1967\):) Tj
T*
(   Proposes that mitochondria and chloroplasts originated as free-living prokaryotic endosymbionts) Tj
T*
(   engulfed by primitive ancestral host cells:) Tj
T*
(   - Mitochondria: Arose ~1.8 billion years ago from an aerobic Alphaproteobacterium engulfed by) Tj
T*
(   an Asgard archaeon-related host cell.) Tj
T*
(   - Chloroplasts: Arose ~1.5 billion years ago from an autotrophic Cyanobacterium engulfed by an) Tj
T*
(   early heterotrophic eukaryote \(primary endosymbiosis\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Structural and Molecular Evidence:) Tj
T*
(   - Double-Membrane Envelope: The inner membrane reflects the original ancestral bacterial plasma) Tj
T*
(   membrane \(rich in cardiolipin, devoid of cholesterol\), while the outer membrane derived from) Tj
T*
(   the host endocytic vacuole.) Tj
T*
(   - Autonomous Genome: Possess circular, double-stranded DNA genomes \(mtDNA, cpDNA\) lacking) Tj
T*
(   histones, replicated by bacterial-like DNA polymerases \(Pol gamma\).) Tj
T*
(   - Bacterial-like Ribosomes: Contain 70S ribosomes \(consisting of 50S and 30S subunits\)) Tj
T*
(   sensitive to bacterial translation inhibitors \(chloramphenicol, streptomycin\), but resistant to) Tj
T*
(   eukaryotic cytosolic 80S inhibitors \(cycloheximide\).) Tj
T*
(   - Formylmethionine: Polypeptide translation initiates with N-formylmethionine \(fMet\).) Tj
T*
(   - Division by Binary Fission: Replicate independently of host mitosis using bacterial division) Tj
T*
(   machinery \(FtsZ homologs in chloroplasts; Dnm1/Drp1 dynamin-related GTPases in mitochondria\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Gene Transfer to the Host Nucleus:) Tj
T*
(   Over evolutionary time, > 95% of the original endosymbiont genes were translocated to the host) Tj
T*
(   nucleus via endosymbiotic gene transfer \(EGT\). Nuclear-encoded organellar proteins are) Tj
T*
(   synthesized on cytosolic ribosomes with N-terminal transit peptides and imported) Tj
T*
(   post-translationally via TOM/TIM or TOC/TIC translocons.) Tj
T*
