(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the protein import machinery of the Outer and Inner Mitochondrial Membranes \(TOM, TIM23, TIM22, and SAM complexes\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Mitochondrial Protein Import Translocase Machineries:) Tj
T*
(   1. Presequence Recognition and Outer Membrane Translocation \(TOM Complex\):) Tj
T*
(   - Most mitochondrial proteins \(~1,500\) are encoded in the nucleus and synthesized as precursors) Tj
T*
(   with an N-terminal, positively charged amphipathic alpha-helical presequence.) Tj
T*
(   - Cytosolic chaperones \(Hsp70\) deliver unfolded precursors to outer membrane receptors Tom20) Tj
T*
(   and Tom22.) Tj
T*
(   - The preprotein is threaded through the central beta-barrel pore of Tom40.) Tj
T*
(   2. Insertion into Outer Membrane \(SAM Complex\):) Tj
T*
(   Outer membrane beta-barrel proteins \(e.g., Porin/VDAC, Tom40\) pass through TOM into the IMS,) Tj
T*
(   bind small Tim chaperones \(Tim9-Tim10\), and are inserted into the outer membrane by the SAM) Tj
T*
(   \(Sorting and Assembly Machinery / Tob51\) complex.) Tj
T*
(   3. Matrix Targeting via TIM23:) Tj
T*
(   - Presequence-carrying proteins emerging from Tom40 are captured by the Tim23/Tim17 complex in) Tj
T*
(   the inner membrane.) Tj
T*
(   - Translocation across the inner membrane is electrophoretically driven by the electrical) Tj
T*
(   membrane potential Delta Psi \(pulling the positive presequence into the negative matrix\).) Tj
T*
(   - As the chain emerges into the matrix, the ATP-driven import motor PAM \(Presequence) Tj
T*
(   Translocase-Associated Motor, containing mtHsp70 and Tim44\) pulls the precursor into the matrix) Tj
T*
(   via an ATP-hydrolyzing ratchet mechanism.) Tj
T*
(   - Mitochondrial Processing Peptidase \(MPP\) cleaves off the presequence.) Tj
T*
