(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the architecture and enzymatic regulation of the Pyruvate Dehydrogenase \(PDH\) Complex, detailing all cofactors and covalent modifications.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Pyruvate Dehydrogenase \(PDH\) Multi-Enzyme Complex:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   A massive macromolecular machine \(~9 MDa\) in the mitochondrial matrix bridging glycolysis to) Tj
T*
(   the TCA cycle:) Tj
T*
(   - E1 \(Pyruvate Dehydrogenase\): A heterotetramer \(alpha2-beta2\) using Thiamine Pyrophosphate) Tj
T*
(   \(TPP\) as prosthetic group.) Tj
T*
(   - E2 \(Dihydrolipoyl Transacetylase\): Forms a structural core of 60 subunits \(in mammals\) with) Tj
T*
(   flexible swinging lipoamide arms.) Tj
T*
(   - E3 \(Dihydrolipoyl Dehydrogenase\): A homodimer containing Flavin Adenine Dinucleotide \(FAD\)) Tj
T*
(   and a redox-active disulfide bond.) Tj
T*
