(   2. Five Sequential Chemical Steps and Cofactors:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: E1 decarboxylates pyruvate, transferring the 2C hydroxyethyl group to TPP, releasing) Tj
T*
(   CO2.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: E1 oxidizes the hydroxyethyl group to an acetyl group and transfers it to the) Tj
T*
(   disulfide bond of lipoamide on the swinging arm of E2.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: E2 transfers the acetyl group from lipoamide to Coenzyme A \(CoA-SH\), releasing) Tj
T*
(   high-energy Acetyl-CoA.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: The reduced, dithiol lipoamide arm swings to E3, where it is re-oxidized by E3's) Tj
T*
(   disulfide bond, restoring lipoamide.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5: The dithiol of E3 transfers electrons to FAD, forming FADH2, which in turn reduces) Tj
T*
(   NAD+ to NADH + H+.) Tj
T*
(   3. Covalent Phosphorylation/Dephosphorylation Regulation:) Tj
T*
(   - Inactivation: Pyruvate Dehydrogenase Kinase \(PDK\) phosphorylates three specific serine) Tj
T*
(   residues on the E1-alpha subunit \(Ser-264, Ser-271, Ser-203\), completely inactivating the) Tj
T*
(   complex. PDK is allosterically activated by high energy charge: [NADH]/[NAD+],) Tj
T*
(   [Acetyl-CoA]/[CoA], and [ATP]/[ADP].) Tj
T*
(   - Activation: Pyruvate Dehydrogenase Phosphatase \(PDP\) dephosphorylates E1-alpha, restoring) Tj
T*
(   full activity. PDP is activated by Ca2+ \(signaling muscle contraction\) and insulin \(signaling) Tj
T*
(   energy abundance\).) Tj
