(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Glycerol-3-Phosphate and Malate-Aspartate shuttles for translocating cytosolic reducing equivalents into mitochondria.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Mitochondrial Shuttles for Cytosolic NADH Translocation:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Problem:) Tj
T*
(   Glycolysis in the cytosol generates 2 NADH per glucose. However, the inner mitochondrial) Tj
T*
(   membrane is strictly impermeable to NADH and NAD+. To be oxidized by the electron transport) Tj
T*
(   chain, reducing equivalents must be shuttled across via metabolic carriers.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Glycerol-3-Phosphate Shuttle \(Skeletal Muscle & Brain\):) Tj
T*
(   - Cytosolic Reaction: Cytosolic glycerol-3-phosphate dehydrogenase oxidizes cytosolic NADH,) Tj
T*
(   reducing Dihydroxyacetone Phosphate \(DHAP\) to Glycerol-3-Phosphate \(G-3-P\).) Tj
T*
(   - Mitochondrial Membrane Reaction: G-3-P diffuses across the outer membrane into the IMS and is) Tj
T*
(   re-oxidized back to DHAP by Mitochondrial Glycerol-3-Phosphate Dehydrogenase, an enzyme) Tj
T*
(   embedded in the outer face of the inner membrane that uses FAD as its prosthetic group.) Tj
T*
(   - FAD is reduced to FADH2, which transfers electrons directly to Ubiquinone \(CoQ\) in the inner) Tj
T*
(   membrane, entering the ETC at Complex III.) Tj
T*
(   - Energetic Yield: Bypasses Complex I; yields only 1.5 ATP per cytosolic NADH \(faster, but) Tj
T*
(   lower thermodynamic efficiency\).) Tj
T*
(   3. The Malate-Aspartate Shuttle \(Heart, Liver & Kidneys\):) Tj
T*
(   - Cytosolic Reduction: Cytosolic Malate Dehydrogenase \(cMDH\) uses cytosolic NADH to reduce) Tj
T*
(   Oxaloacetate to Malate.) Tj
T*
(   - Transport: The Malate-alpha-Ketoglutarate Antiporter translocates Malate into the matrix in) Tj
T*
(   exchange for alpha-ketoglutarate.) Tj
T*
(   - Matrix Oxidation: Mitochondrial Malate Dehydrogenase \(mMDH\) oxidizes Malate back to) Tj
T*
(   Oxaloacetate, generating Matrix NADH from matrix NAD+!) Tj
T*
(   - Transamination & Recycling: Matrix Oxaloacetate transaminates with glutamate via Aspartate) Tj
T*
(   Aminotransferase \(AST\) to yield Aspartate and alpha-ketoglutarate. The Glutamate-Aspartate) Tj
T*
(   Antiporter translocates Aspartate out to the cytosol in exchange for glutamate, completing the) Tj
T*
(   cycle.) Tj
T*
(   - Energetic Yield: Delivers electrons directly to Complex I, yielding 2.5 ATP per cytosolic) Tj
T*
(   NADH \(maximum energetic yield\).) Tj
T*
