(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the genetic organization of Human Mitochondrial DNA \(mtDNA\), its transcription mechanism, and maternal inheritance pattern.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Human Mitochondrial Genome Organization and Expression:) Tj
T*
(   1. Genomic Organization:) Tj
T*
(   - Size and Topology: A circular, double-stranded DNA molecule of 16,569 base pairs.) Tj
T*
(   - Strand Asymmetry: Consists of a purine-rich Heavy \(H\) strand and a pyrimidine-rich Light \(L\)) Tj
T*
(   strand, separable by density gradient centrifugation.) Tj
T*
(   - Coding Content: Contains 37 genes:) Tj
T*
(   - 13 essential polypeptides encoding core respiratory chain subunits \(7 in Complex I, 1 in) Tj
T*
(   Complex III, 3 in Complex IV, 2 in Complex V\).) Tj
T*
(   - 2 ribosomal RNAs \(12S and 16S rRNA\).) Tj
T*
(   - 22 transfer RNAs \(tRNAs\) required for intramitochondrial translation.) Tj
T*
(   - Extreme Genetic Economy: Lacks introns completely; possesses no non-coding intergenic) Tj
T*
(   regions; several termination codons are incomplete \(U or UA\) and created post-transcriptionally) Tj
T*
(   by polyadenylation!) Tj
T*
(   2. Non-Coding Control Region \(D-Loop\):) Tj
T*
(   A ~1.1 kb region containing the Origin of Heavy-Strand Replication \(O_H\) and the Heavy-Strand) Tj
