(   Homologous to mitochondrial ATP synthase, CF0CF1 is localized exclusively in non-appressed) Tj
T*
(   thylakoid stroma lamellae and grana margins:) Tj
T*
(   - CF0 \(Membrane Domain\): Composed of subunits I, II, IV, and a large ring of 14 hydrophobic III) Tj
T*
(   \(c\) subunits \(c14 ring\).) Tj
T*
(   - CF1 \(Stromal Catalytic Head\): A hexamer of alternating alpha and beta subunits,) Tj
T*
(   \(alpha-beta\)3, connected to the c14 ring via central rotor stalk gamma and epsilon subunits.) Tj
T*
(   2. Functional Consequence of the Large c14 Ring:) Tj
T*
(   Because the c-ring contains 14 subunits, one 360-degree rotation translocates 14 protons and) Tj
T*
(   produces 3 ATP:) Tj
T*
(   - H+/ATP ratio = 14 / 3 = 4.67 H+ per ATP!) Tj
T*
(   - This high stoichiometric proton requirement reflects the large electrochemical pH gradient) Tj
T*
(   \(Delta pH ~ 3 units, lumen pH ~ 5.0 vs stroma pH ~ 8.0\) and virtually zero Delta Psi in) Tj
T*
(   steady-state chloroplasts \(due to counter-ion Cl- and Mg2+ fluxes\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Unique Light-Dependent Redox Regulation:) Tj
T*
(   Unlike mitochondria, which operate continuously, chloroplast ATP synthase must be shut down in) Tj
T*
(   the dark to prevent wasteful reverse hydrolysis of stromal ATP:) Tj
T*
(   - The gamma subunit of CF1 possesses a unique 38-amino-acid insertion containing two conserved) Tj
T*
(   cysteine residues \(Cys-199 and Cys-205\).) Tj
T*
(   - In the dark: The cysteines form an intramolecular disulfide bond \(S-S\), locking the gamma) Tj
T*
(   subunit in an inactive conformation.) Tj
T*
(   - In the light: Photosynthetic electron transport reduces Ferredoxin. Ferredoxin-Thioredoxin) Tj
T*
(   Reductase \(FTR\) transfers electrons to Thioredoxin-m, which reduces the CF1-gamma disulfide) Tj
T*
(   bond to free sulfhydryls \(-SH HS-\), unlocking rotation and activating ATP synthesis.) Tj
