(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the metabolic pathway and enzymatic regulation of the Pentose Phosphate Pathway \(PPP\) in producing NADPH for biosynthesis.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Pentose Phosphate Pathway \(Hexose Monophosphate Shunt\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Physiological Objectives:) Tj
T*
(   - Generation of NADPH: The primary cellular reducing currency required for reductive) Tj
T*
(   biosynthesis \(fatty acids, cholesterol, steroid hormones\) and for maintaining reduced) Tj
T*
(   glutathione \(GSH\) to resist oxidative stress.) Tj
T*
(   - Generation of Ribose-5-Phosphate: Essential five-carbon sugar backbone for nucleotide, RNA,) Tj
T*
(   and DNA synthesis.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Oxidative Irreversible Phase \(NADPH Production\):) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Glucose-6-Phosphate Dehydrogenase \(G6PD\) oxidizes Glucose-6-Phosphate to) Tj
T*
(   6-Phosphoglucono-delta-lactone, reducing NADP+ to NADPH + H+.) Tj
T*
(   * Regulatory Checkpoint: G6PD is the rate-limiting committed enzyme; allosterically inhibited) Tj
T*
(   by high [NADPH]/[NADP+] ratios.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: 6-Phosphogluconolactonase hydrolyzes the lactone to 6-Phosphogluconate.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: 6-Phosphogluconate Dehydrogenase oxidatively decarboxylates 6-phosphogluconate to) Tj
T*
(   Ribulose-5-Phosphate, generating a second molecule of NADPH and releasing CO2.) Tj
T*
(   - Yield: 2 NADPH per G-6-P oxidized.) Tj
T*
(   3. The Non-Oxidative Reversible Phase \(Carbon Shuffling\):) Tj
T*
(   Reversibly interconverts pentose phosphates \(ribulose-5-P, xylulose-5-P, ribose-5-P\) into) Tj
T*
(   glycolytic intermediates \(fructose-6-P and glyceraldehyde-3-P\) using two key enzymes:) Tj
T*
(   - Transketolase: A Thiamine Pyrophosphate \(TPP\)-dependent enzyme transferring 2-carbon units.) Tj
T*
(   - Transaldolase: Uses an active-site lysine Schiff base to transfer 3-carbon units.) Tj
T*
(   4. Clinical Relevance \(G6PD Deficiency\):) Tj
T*
(   The most common human enzymatic disorder \(~400 million people, X-linked recessive\).) Tj
T*
(   Erythrocytes lack mitochondria and rely exclusively on G6PD for NADPH. Deficiency leaves RBCs) Tj
T*
(   vulnerable to oxidative stress from antimalarial drugs \(primaquine\) or fava beans, causing) Tj
T*
