(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the biochemical mechanisms of Cytochrome c release during Apoptosis and the assembly of the Apoptosome.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Mitochondrial Apoptotic Pathway and Apoptosome Assembly:) Tj
T*
(   1. Upstream Pro-Apoptotic Signaling:) Tj
T*
(   Intracellular stress \(DNA damage, oncogene activation, withdrawal of survival factors\)) Tj
T*
(   activates BH3-only proteins \(Bim, Bid, Puma, Noxa\):) Tj
T*
(   - BH3-only proteins neutralize anti-apoptotic Bcl-2 and Bcl-xL.) Tj
T*
(   - They directly activate multi-domain pro-apoptotic effectors Bax and Bak.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mitochondrial Outer Membrane Permeabilization \(MOMP\):) Tj
T*
(   Activated Bax and Bak oligomerize into high-order toroidal proteolipidic pores spanning the) Tj
T*
(   outer mitochondrial membrane. MOMP allows the indiscriminate escape of proteins residing in the) Tj
T*
(   intermembrane space into the cytosol:) Tj
T*
(   - Cytochrome c, Smac/DIABLO, Omi/HtrA2, Endonuclease G, and AIF.) Tj
T*
(   3. Apoptosome Assembly:) Tj
T*
(   In the cytoplasm, released Cytochrome c binds to the WD40 domain of Apaf-1 \(Apoptotic Protease) Tj
T*
(   Activating Factor-1\):) Tj
T*
(   - In the presence of dATP or ATP, Cytochrome c binding induces an extensive conformational) Tj
T*
(   reorganization of Apaf-1, exposing its central nucleotide-binding and oligomerization domain) Tj
T*
(   \(NOD\) and N-terminal Caspase Activation and Recruitment Domain \(CARD\).) Tj
T*
(   - Seven Apaf-1-Cytochrome c-dATP complexes oligomerize into a wheel-like, heptameric) Tj
T*
(   macromolecular platform \(~700 kDa\) termed the Apoptosome.) Tj
T*
(   4. Caspase Cascade Activation:) Tj
T*
(   - The central hub of the apoptosome presents seven CARD domains that recruit inactive initiator) Tj
T*
(   Procaspase-9 via homotypic CARD-CARD interactions.) Tj
T*
(   - Forced dimerization on the apoptosome platform activates Caspase-9 without cleavage.) Tj
T*
(   - Active Caspase-9 proteolytically cleaves and activates downstream executioner caspases:) Tj
T*
(   Caspase-3 and Caspase-7.) Tj
T*
(   - Executioner caspases cleave hundreds of cellular structural and functional proteins \(ICAD,) Tj
T*
(   lamins, PARP\), executing apoptotic cell death.) Tj
T*
