(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the molecular mechanisms of Mitochondrial Dynamics \(Fusion and Fission\) and explain the roles of Mfn1, Mfn2, Opa1, and Drp1.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Mitochondrial Dynamics: Fusion, Fission, and Quality Control:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physiological Role:) Tj
T*
(   Mitochondria are not static individual beans; they form a continuously remodeling, dynamic) Tj
T*
(   reticular network regulated by opposing fusion and fission machineries, essential for) Tj
T*
(   maintaining metabolic efficiency, sharing mtDNA, and isolating damaged segments for mitophagy.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mitochondrial Fusion Machinery:) Tj
T*
(   - Outer Membrane Fusion \(Mitofusins\): Mfn1 and Mfn2 are large GTPases anchored in the outer) Tj
T*
(   membrane by two transmembrane segments, with both N- and C-terminal heptad repeat domains \(HR1,) Tj
T*
(   HR2\) facing the cytosol. Trans-dimerization of Mfn1/2 complexes on opposing mitochondria) Tj
T*
(   hydrolyzes GTP, pulling outer membranes into close proximity to drive lipid mixing.) Tj
T*
(   - Inner Membrane Fusion \(Opa1\): Optic Atrophy 1 \(Opa1\) is a dynamin-related GTPase localized in) Tj
T*
(   the IMS. The long membrane-anchored form \(L-Opa1\) pairs with the short soluble form \(S-Opa1,) Tj
T*
(   cleaved by the metalloprotease OMA1/Yme1L\) to tether opposing inner membranes, driving inner) Tj
T*
(   membrane fusion and maintaining narrow cristae junction architecture.) Tj
T*
(   3. Mitochondrial Fission Machinery \(Drp1\):) Tj
T*
(   - Dynamin-Related Protein 1 \(Drp1\): A cytosolic GTPase lacking membrane-targeting domains.) Tj
T*
(   - ER-Marked Constriction: Sites of fission are pre-determined by endoplasmic reticulum tubules) Tj
T*
(   wrapping around the mitochondrion, constricting it to a diameter of ~150 nm via inverted formin) Tj
T*
(   2 \(INF2\)-driven actin polymerization.) Tj
T*
(   - Drp1 Recruitment: Outer membrane receptor proteins \(Mff, Fis1, MiD49, MiD51\) recruit Drp1) Tj
T*
(   from the cytosol to the constricted site.) Tj
T*
(   - Scission: Drp1 oligomerizes into a ring-like spiral collar around the constriction. GTP) Tj
T*
(   hydrolysis drives ring constriction and torsional scission, severing the mitochondrion into two) Tj
T*
(   daughter organelles.) Tj
T*
(   4. Mitophagy Coupling:) Tj
T*
(   Depolarized daughter segments fail to import PINK1 kinase, causing PINK1 accumulation on the) Tj
T*
(   outer membrane, which recruits and activates the E3 ubiquitin ligase Parkin, targeting the) Tj
T*
(   damaged organelle for autophagic destruction \(mitophagy\).) Tj
T*
