(   In Complex IV, the heme a3 iron atom is five-coordinate, presenting an open axial coordination) Tj
T*
(   position designed to bind molecular oxygen \(O2\) between Fe\(II\) and Cu_B\(I\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Mechanism of Cyanide \(CN-\) Poisoning:) Tj
T*
(   - Cyanide anion \(CN-\) is an isoelectronic analog of O2 that diffuses rapidly across membranes.) Tj
T*
(   - CN- binds with extraordinarily high affinity \(Kd ~ 10^-7 M\) to the oxidized ferric [Fe\(III\)]) Tj
T*
(   state of heme a3.) Tj
T*
(   - Coordination of cyanide permanently locks the binuclear center in a rigid, non-functional) Tj
T*
(   coordination geometry, completely blocking electron transfer from heme a to heme a3 and) Tj
T*
(   preventing oxygen reduction to water.) Tj
T*
(   3. Mechanism of Carbon Monoxide \(CO\) Poisoning:) Tj
T*
(   - Carbon monoxide binds specifically to the reduced ferrous [Fe\(II\)] state of heme a3, directly) Tj
T*
(   competing with O2.) Tj
T*
(   - While CO's primary toxicity stems from high-affinity binding to hemoglobin \(forming) Tj
T*
(   carboxyhemoglobin, left-shifting the O2 dissociation curve\), its direct inhibition of Complex) Tj
T*
(   IV contributes significantly to cellular histotoxic hypoxia in high-metabolic tissues \(brain) Tj
T*
(   and myocardium\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Mechanism of Azide \(N3-\) Poisoning:) Tj
T*
(   - Azide binds to both Fe\(III\) of heme a3 and Cu_B, bridging the two metal centers and halting) Tj
T*
(   the catalytic cycle identically to cyanide.) Tj
T*
(   5. Physiological Consequences and Antidote Biochemistry:) Tj
T*
(   - Complete inhibition of Complex IV halts electron flow throughout the entire respiratory chain) Tj
T*
(   \(Complexes I-III become fully reduced\).) Tj
T*
(   - Proton pumping ceases; the proton motive force collapses; ATP synthesis stops immediately.) Tj
T*
(   - Cells shift to anaerobic glycolysis, producing massive lactic acidosis and rapid cytotoxic) Tj
T*
(   edema.) Tj
T*
(   - Antidote Therapy: Administration of Hydroxocobalamin \(Vitamin B12a\) binds cyanide with higher) Tj
T*
(   affinity than heme a3, forming non-toxic Cyanocobalamin excreted in urine; or Sodium Nitrite,) Tj
T*
(   which oxidizes hemoglobin to methemoglobin [Fe\(III\)], sequestering cyanide away from) Tj
T*
(   mitochondria.) Tj
