(   4. Receptor Ubiquitination and Recycling:) Tj
T*
(   - Following cargo release, PEX5 is mono-ubiquitinated at a conserved cysteine residue \(Cys-11\)) Tj
T*
(   by the membrane-bound ubiquitin-conjugating enzyme PEX4 \(E2\) and RING-finger ligases PEX2,) Tj
T*
(   PEX10, PEX12 \(E3\).) Tj
T*
(   - The hexameric AAA+ ATPase complex PEX1-PEX6 utilizes ATP hydrolysis to pull) Tj
T*
(   mono-ubiquitinated PEX5 out of the peroxisomal membrane back into the cytosol, where it is) Tj
T*
(   de-ubiquitinated and recycled.) Tj
T*
(   5. Clinical Disorder \(Zellweger Syndrome\):) Tj
T*
(   Mutations in PEX genes \(most commonly PEX1\) abolish peroxisome biogenesis, leaving empty) Tj
T*
(   peroxisomal 'ghosts'. Severe accumulation of very long-chain fatty acids \(VLCFAs\) causes) Tj
T*
(   craniofacial dysmorphism, hypotonia, hepatomegaly, and infant death.) Tj
