(   [Problem Statement]: Explain how the ATP/ADP ratio and energy charge govern coordinate allosteric regulation of Glycolysis and the Citric Acid Cycle.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Coordinate Allosteric Regulation by Adenylate Energy Charge:) Tj
T*
(   1. Concept of Energy Charge \(Atkinson Formulation\):) Tj
T*
(   Energy Charge = \( [ATP] + 0.5 * [ADP] \) / \( [ATP] + [ADP] + [AMP] \).) Tj
T*
(   In healthy eukaryotic cells, energy charge is maintained within a narrow physiological window) Tj
T*
(   between 0.85 and 0.95.) Tj
T*
(   2. Master Checkpoints in Glycolysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Phosphofructokinase-1 \(PFK-1\): The primary committed gatekeeper of glycolysis.) Tj
T*
(   - Allosteric Inhibition: High concentrations of ATP bind to a low-affinity allosteric site) Tj
T*
(   outside the catalytic pocket, stabilizing the low-affinity T-state. Citrate \(indicating TCA) Tj
T*
(   cycle saturation\) potentiates ATP inhibition.) Tj
T*
(   - Allosteric Activation: Elevated AMP \(reflecting ATP depletion via adenylate kinase: 2 ADP <->) Tj
T*
(   ATP + AMP\) and Fructose-2,6-bisphosphate relieve ATP inhibition, shifting PFK-1 to the) Tj
T*
(   high-affinity R-state.) Tj
T*
(   - Pyruvate Kinase: Allosterically inhibited by ATP and alanine; activated by feed-forward) Tj
T*
(   stimulation from fructose-1,6-bisphosphate.) Tj
T*
(   3. Master Checkpoints in the Citric Acid Cycle:) Tj
T*
(   - Citrate Synthase: Inhibited by ATP, NADH, and succinyl-CoA \(feedback inhibition\).) Tj
T*
(   - Isocitrate Dehydrogenase \(ICDH\): Strongly allosterically activated by ADP, which lowers the) Tj
T*
(   Km for isocitrate by 10-fold; strongly inhibited by ATP and NADH.) Tj
T*
(   - Alpha-Ketoglutarate Dehydrogenase Complex: Structurally and mechanistically homologous to) Tj
T*
(   PDH; inhibited by its direct products \(succinyl-CoA and NADH\) and high ATP.) Tj
T*
(   4. Coordinated Metabolic Logic:) Tj
T*
(   When ATP is depleted and ADP/AMP rise \(energy deficit\): PFK-1 and ICDH are maximally activated,) Tj
T*
(   accelerating glycolytic flux and TCA cycle turnover to replenish ATP. Conversely, when ATP and) Tj
T*
(   NADH accumulate \(energy surplus\): all upstream regulatory enzymes are allosterically) Tj
T*
(   suppressed, shunting glucose-6-phosphate into glycogen storage or the pentose phosphate) Tj
T*
(   pathway.) Tj
T*
