(   the monoepoxide Antheraxanthin, and finally to the epoxide-free Zeaxanthin during) Tj
T*
(   photoprotective Non-Photochemical Quenching \(NPQ\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Domain Organization:) Tj
T*
(   - N-terminal Cysteine-Rich Domain: Contains 13 conserved cysteine residues involved in) Tj
T*
(   essential intramolecular disulfide bonds stabilizing protein folding.) Tj
T*
(   - Central Lipocalin Domain: Forms an 8-stranded antiparallel beta-barrel possessing a) Tj
T*
(   hydrophobic cavity that accommodates the bulky, hydrophobic beta-ionone ring and polyene tail) Tj
T*
(   of the xanthophyll substrate.) Tj
T*
(   - C-terminal Glutamate-Rich Domain: Contains a high density of acidic glutamate and aspartate) Tj
T*
(   residues acting as the primary pH-sensor.) Tj
T*
(   3. Strict pH-Dependent Conformational Switch:) Tj
T*
(   - In the dark or low light \(lumen pH ~ 7.0 to 7.2\): VDE exists as an inactive, soluble monomer) Tj
T*
(   freely diffusing in the aqueous thylakoid lumen. Its negatively charged C-terminal glutamate) Tj
T*
(   residues cause electrostatic repulsion, preventing membrane binding.) Tj
T*
(   - Under high light \(lumen pH drops below 5.5\): Protonation of the glutamate residues) Tj
T*
(   neutralizes negative surface charges. VDE undergoes dimerization and conformational) Tj
T*
(   rearrangement, exposing hydrophobic surface patches that drive reversible electrostatic and) Tj
T*
(   hydrophobic binding to the thylakoid lipid bilayer.) Tj
T*
(   4. Cofactor Requirement \(Ascorbic Acid\):) Tj
T*
(   - In the active membrane-bound dimer state, VDE requires Ascorbic Acid \(Vitamin C\) as an) Tj
T*
(   obligatory co-substrate.) Tj
T*
(   - Ascorbate binds to the active site, serving as the two-electron donor that reduces the) Tj
T*
(   epoxide oxygen, liberating it as water and generating dehydroascorbate, which is subsequently) Tj
T*
(   regenerated in the stroma by the ascorbate-glutathione cycle.) Tj
T*
(   - The resulting zeaxanthin molecules accumulate in the light-harvesting antenna complexes,) Tj
T*
(   directly quenching singlet excited chlorophylls to dissipate excess solar energy safely as) Tj
T*
(   heat.) Tj
T*
